00:10:30,559 --> 00:10:32,752
Progressive reports that its average

293
00:10:32,752 --> 00:10:35,383
personal auto premium per policy is

294
00:10:35,383 --> 00:10:36,422
falling.

295
00:10:36,684 --> 00:10:38,734
Let me draw the cycle.

296
00:10:38,834 --> 00:10:40,886
Costs rise faster than prices,

297
00:10:40,886 --> 00:10:43,304
and insurers lose money.

298
00:10:43,414 --> 00:10:45,259
Insurers raise prices,

299
00:10:45,259 --> 00:10:46,394
sharply.

300
00:10:46,474 --> 00:10:47,581
Costs cool down,

301
00:10:47,581 --> 00:10:50,108
but prices are already high,

302
00:10:50,108 --> 00:10:51,844
and profits soar.

303
00:10:52,044 --> 00:10:54,684
Then competition and regulators push

304
00:10:54,684 --> 00:10:56,244
prices back down.

305
00:10:56,334 --> 00:10:58,911
Drivers live through the expensive part of

306
00:10:58,911 --> 00:11:00,541
every turn.

307
00:11:00,784 --> 00:11:03,055
So why did your car insurance get

308
00:11:03,055 --> 00:11:04,664
so expensive?

309
00:11:04,794 --> 00:11:07,020
More expensive cars and repairs,

310
00:11:07,020 --> 00:11:08,246
deadlier crashes,

311
00:11:08,246 --> 00:11:10,722
rising legal and medical costs,

312
00:11:10,722 --> 00:11:13,473
and insurers who raised prices fast to

313
00:11:13,473 --> 00:11:15,574
make up for their losses.

314
00:11:15,614 --> 00:11:18,044
Prices are finally easing.

315
00:11:18,094 --> 00:11:20,087
But they remain far above where they

316
00:11:20,087 --> 00:11:21,837
were before the pandemic,

317
00:11:21,837 --> 00:11:23,609
and the next turn of the cycle

318
00:11:23,609 --> 00:11:25,538
is never far away.

319
00:11:25,784 --> 00:11:27,868
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

320
00:11:27,868 --> 00:11:30,354
we follow the money behind another hidden

321
00:11:30,354 --> 00:11:32,484
link of the world economy.

322
00:11:32,634 --> 00:11:34,560
This is The Hidden Economics.
